{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/527773-stealing-dead-life-the-ordo-dracul-and-the-deathless-mummies","id":527773,"title":"Stealing Dead Life-The Ordo Dracul and the Deathless Mummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T09:43:47-07:00","id":527773,"title":"Stealing Dead Life-The Ordo Dracul and the Deathless Mummies","content":"So, you're a Dragon wanting to become a new and better class of monster. You've discovered the Deathless(Arisen or Deceived, who cares), maybe even captured one or two, and you're starting to figure out some of their secrets. Yeah, your work is supposed to expose secrets of the Blood, but you think you graft some ideas here and there. Particularly the stars you get from this one freak.<br /> <br /> What secrets to do you rip out of them to make your scaley hide? What traits do you coil around your curses?<br /> <br /> (Nevermind that I don't think this is actually possible because of the blood focus, just run with it and toss ideas out there)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:53:26-07:00","id":527795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/527773-stealing-dead-life-the-ordo-dracul-and-the-deathless-mummies#post527773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you're a Dragon wanting to become a new and better class of monster. You've discovered the Deathless(Arisen or Deceived, who cares), maybe even captured one or two, and you're starting to figure out some of their secrets. Yeah, your work is supposed to expose secrets of the Blood, but you think you graft some ideas here and there. Particularly the stars you get from this one freak.<br /> <br /> What secrets to do you rip out of them to make your scaley hide? What traits do you coil around your curses?<br /> <br /> (Nevermind that I don't think this is actually possible because of the blood focus, just run with it and toss ideas out there)</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely to learn such traits of the aftermath of an encounter.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that trying to hold things that can shoot great balls of flaming flying rocks at you while still in your haven is generally not a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:14:58-07:00","id":527816,"title":"","content":"You make it work. if Last Dynasty International can make it work, you can.<br /> <br /> Look, it's not like I have an exact scenario here, I'm just curious what people think an Ordo Dracul member would take away from research on the Deathless and how that might manifest as a field of study(Coils and Scales)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:41:56-07:00","id":527859,"title":"","content":"Maybe some sort of Mystery dealing with Torpor? Like, something that allows you to use it in order to &quot;shift&quot; your mind and Curse into another corpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:29:05-07:00","id":527996,"title":"","content":"Torpor sounds like the best route, with the ability to come out of it with higher BP being the obvious idea. Another one is making anything less than atomisation throwing you into torpor, even if it should have killed you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:19:57-07:00","id":528488,"title":"","content":"Something to do with Torpor, maybe something to do with Sekhem, Blood Potency and Torpor.<br /> <br /> I think there's obvious potential in the concept of Sekhem as it relates to Vitae, and how it might render the blood more potent. I could imagine a Scale that causes a big burst of sudden Blood Potency and power, which dwindles over time, and could potentially result in a vampire going into torpor, as one example of experimenting with Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Scale consumes a relic to offer a massive but temporary boost to Blood Potency?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't know how it works mechanically in Mummy, but I know occult geometry and ley lines play a role there. Maybe one of these places of power could be a Wyrm's Nest for the Ordo, or worse, whatever strange beastie might be there could be controlled or bonded through Vitae + Some kind of fontal ritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-26-2015, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:08:34-07:00","id":528540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/527773-stealing-dead-life-the-ordo-dracul-and-the-deathless-mummies?p=528488#post528488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to do with Torpor, maybe something to do with Sekhem, Blood Potency and Torpor.<br /> <br /> I think there's obvious potential in the concept of Sekhem as it relates to Vitae, and how it might render the blood more potent. I could imagine a Scale that causes a big burst of sudden Blood Potency and power, which dwindles over time, and could potentially result in a vampire going into torpor, as one example of experimenting with Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Scale consumes a relic to offer a massive but temporary boost to Blood Potency?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't know how it works mechanically in Mummy, <b>but I know occult geometry and ley lines play a role there.</b> Maybe one of these places of power could be a Wyrm's Nest for the Ordo, or worse, whatever strange beastie might be there could be controlled or bonded through Vitae + Some kind of fontal ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I forgot that the Ordo deals with that stuff. Yeah, stuff along those lines is welcome to.<br /> <br /> God, that actually works really well with the thought I had just had half an hour ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:26:29-07:00","id":528548,"title":"","content":"Do share the thought!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(when you can/feel like it)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:44:04-07:00","id":528552,"title":"","content":"Very soon I'm going to be beginning a series of games that take place in Paris(or at least use it as a homebase, or in the case of Demon, a prominent side location). At this point, I don't want to plan too much for each of the lines, particularly since I don't want to run all of them, but I want a few strands for each to keep in mind for when I get around to it. This thread started as an idle thought of how I can tie in a vampire element to the end goal of those exercises.<br /> <br /> Unrelated to that, I was idly picking through bits of the cities lore when I came across the Paris Meridian-the thing Dan Brown lied about and called the Rose Line, you know- and found out that, actually, yeah, there's an occult conspiracy theory about the Paris Meridian, and that in fact one guy called it &quot;the heart of the devil&quot;. That struck me as interesting for sort of parallel for vampires, this vein of darkness through the city, and it got me thinking about the flow of blood and Strix and such. I hadn't quite worked out how it was going to all work out, because I need characters to build a story, but I like that as a device so much that I went ahead and named the potential Vampire game &quot;The Rose Line&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then I got reminded about this, and the fates aligned. It doesn't hurt that as a meridian it carries some astronomical implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-26-2015, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}